IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `cpp-core`

-- Canada Pension Plan Regulations (C.R.C., c. 385), PART I (part): regulations 3 to 7 -- the definitions of
-- Part I, the computation of the employee's contribution, the provincial pension plan, the employer's
-- contribution. Piece cr1. LAYER 1: the law as the text states it.
--
-- Money is a NUMBER of dollars; a rate is a fraction (5% is 0.05). The rates, the basic exemption and the
-- maximum pensionable earnings are fixed by the Act (sections 11.1, 11.2, 18, 18.1 and 19/20, piece cp1), not
-- by these Regulations, so they arrive as one record of inputs (`cr1 Figures the Act sets for a year`).
-- Nothing in this module states a rate for any year. The rates in the tests are invented, round numbers.
--
-- Regulation 5 rounds "to the nearest multiple of $0.01 or, if that result is equidistant from two such
-- multiples, to the higher of them": round half up, also for a negative number. The prelude ROUND rounds
-- half to even, so it is not used.

§ `Regulations, Part I -- computation of the employee's contribution (regs 3 to 7)`

§§ `The figures the Act sets, and the facts about the pay`

-- out of range: sections 11.1 and 11.2 (the rates), 17, 18 (maximum pensionable earnings), 17.1, 18.1
-- (additional maximum pensionable earnings), 19 and 20 (basic exemption) -- piece cp1
DECLARE `cr1 Figures the Act sets for a year` HAS
    `the contribution rate for employees` IS A NUMBER
    `the first additional contribution rate for employees` IS A NUMBER
    `the second additional contribution rate for employees` IS A NUMBER
    `the basic exemption` IS A NUMBER
    `the maximum pensionable earnings` IS A NUMBER
    `the additional maximum pensionable earnings` IS A NUMBER

-- How the employee is ordinarily paid: the headings of the table in regulation 5(5).
-- src:85 | (5) For the purposes of subsection (2), the amount of an employee’s basic exemption for each pay period in a year is
-- src:86 | (a) in the case of an employee who is ordinarily paid
-- src:87 | (i) hourly, $1.75,
-- src:88 | (ii) daily, $14.58,
-- src:89 | (iii) weekly, $67.30,
-- src:90 | (iv) bi-weekly, $134.61,
-- src:91 | (v) quadri-weekly, $269.23,
-- src:92 | (vi) semi-monthly, $145.83,
-- src:93 | (vii) monthly, $291.66,
-- src:94 | (viii) quarterly, $875,
-- src:95 | (ix) semi-annually, $1,750, or
-- src:96 | (x) annually, $3,500;
-- src:97 | (b) in the case of an employee who is ordinarily paid only in respect of a period of 10 months in the year and is paid
-- src:98 | (i) in 22 payments, $159.09,
-- src:99 | (ii) semi-monthly, $175, or
-- src:100 | (iii) monthly, $350; and
-- src:101 | (c) in any other case, the amount that is the greater of
-- src:102 | (i) the product obtained when $3,500 is multiplied by the fraction that the number of days in the period is of 365, and
-- src:103 | (ii) $67.30.
@ref Reg 5(5) (src:85-103)
DECLARE `cr1 How an employee is ordinarily paid` IS ONE OF
    `paid hourly`
    `paid daily`
    `paid weekly`
    `paid bi-weekly`
    `paid quadri-weekly`
    `paid semi-monthly`
    `paid monthly`
    `paid quarterly`
    `paid semi-annually`
    `paid annually`
    `paid in 22 payments in respect of a period of 10 months in the year`
    `paid semi-monthly in respect of a period of 10 months in the year`
    `paid monthly in respect of a period of 10 months in the year`
    `paid in any other way`

-- One payment of remuneration for one pay period, from pensionable employment.
DECLARE `cr1 Payment of remuneration` HAS
    `the payment of remuneration from pensionable employment` IS A NUMBER
    `the part of the payment that is ordinary remuneration` IS A NUMBER
    `how the employee is ordinarily paid` IS A `cr1 How an employee is ordinarily paid`
    `the number of days in the pay period` IS A NUMBER
    `the number of pay periods ending in the year` IS A NUMBER

-- What the employer has already done in the year, and what the provincial pension plan has already taken.
DECLARE `cr1 Position earlier in the year` HAS
    `base and first additional contributions already deducted under this Part` IS A NUMBER
    `second additional contributions already deducted under this Part` IS A NUMBER
    `total remuneration the employer has already paid the employee in the year` IS A NUMBER

-- out of range: the provincial pension plans' own rates are not among the texts this encoding reads.
DECLARE `cr1 Provincial pension plan position` HAS
    `the employee has made contributions for the year under a provincial pension plan in respect of salary and wages paid by the employer` IS A BOOLEAN
    `base and first additional contributions already required to be deducted under the provincial pension plan` IS A NUMBER
    `second additional contributions already required to be deducted under the provincial pension plan` IS A NUMBER
    `sum of the provincial plan's contribution rate and first additional contribution rate for employees` IS A NUMBER
    `the provincial plan's second additional contribution rate for employees` IS A NUMBER

§§ `Regulation 3: the definitions of Part I`

-- "remuneration" has the same meaning as "contributory salary and wages" in section 12 of the Act, so every
-- amount of remuneration in this module is that section 12 figure, taken as an input (piece cp1). It needs no
-- rule of its own.
-- src:68 | year’s maximum base contribution means an amount calculated by multiplying a person’s contribution rate for the year by the difference between the amount of the person’s maximum pensionable earnings and the amount of the person’s basic exemption; (cotisation de base maximale pour l’année)
@ref Reg 3 "year's maximum base contribution" (src:68)
GIVEN figures IS A `cr1 Figures the Act sets for a year`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`reg 3 — the year's maximum base contribution` figures MEANS
    (figures's `the contribution rate for employees`)
    TIMES ((figures's `the maximum pensionable earnings`) MINUS (figures's `the basic exemption`))

-- src:70 | year’s maximum first additional contribution means an amount calculated by multiplying a person’s first additional contribution rate for the year by the difference between the amount of the person’s maximum pensionable earnings and the amount of the person’s basic exemption; (première cotisation supplémentaire maximale pour l’année)
@ref Reg 3 "year's maximum first additional contribution" (src:70)
GIVEN figures IS A `cr1 Figures the Act sets for a year`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`reg 3 — the year's maximum first additional contribution` figures MEANS
    (figures's `the first additional contribution rate for employees`)
    TIMES ((figures's `the maximum pensionable earnings`) MINUS (figures's `the basic exemption`))

-- src:71 | year’s maximum second additional contribution means an amount calculated by multiplying a person’s second additional contribution rate for the year by the difference between the amount of the person’s additional maximum pensionable earnings and the amount of the person’s maximum pensionable earnings. (deuxième cotisation supplémentaire maximale pour l’année)
@ref Reg 3 "year's maximum second additional contribution" (src:71)
GIVEN figures IS A `cr1 Figures the Act sets for a year`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`reg 3 — the year's maximum second additional contribution` figures MEANS
    (figures's `the second additional contribution rate for employees`)
    TIMES ((figures's `the additional maximum pensionable earnings`) MINUS (figures's `the maximum pensionable earnings`))

-- ordinary remuneration means the remuneration paid to an employee on a pay day in respect of employment in
-- the relevant pay period, and includes fees paid to a director of a corporation if no other remuneration is
-- payable to the director by the corporation.
-- src:61 | ordinary remuneration means the remuneration paid to an employee on a pay day in respect of employment in the relevant pay period and includes fees paid to a director of a corporation if no other remuneration is payable to the director by the corporation; (rémunération ordinaire)
@ref Reg 3 "ordinary remuneration" (src:61)
GIVEN `remuneration paid to an employee on a pay day in respect of employment in the relevant pay period` IS A BOOLEAN
      `fees paid to a director of a corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `no other remuneration is payable to the director by the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 3 — a payment is ordinary remuneration` `remuneration paid to an employee on a pay day in respect of employment in the relevant pay period` `fees paid to a director of a corporation` `no other remuneration is payable to the director by the corporation` MEANS
        `remuneration paid to an employee on a pay day in respect of employment in the relevant pay period`
    OR  (`fees paid to a director of a corporation` AND `no other remuneration is payable to the director by the corporation`)

-- pay day means the day on which remuneration ordinarily is paid to an employee.
-- src:62 | pay day means the day on which remuneration ordinarily is paid to an employee; (jour de paie)
@ref Reg 3 "pay day" (src:62)
GIVEN day IS A DATE
      `the day on which remuneration ordinarily is paid to the employee` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 3 — a day is a pay day` day `the day on which remuneration ordinarily is paid to the employee` MEANS
    day EQUALS `the day on which remuneration ordinarily is paid to the employee`

-- pay period means (a) the usual period for which an employee is paid on a pay day, or (b) where there is no
-- usual period, the period for which the employee is actually paid on a pay day, and for the purposes of (a)
-- and (b) includes a period of an hour or a day. The length is counted in days, so an hour is 1/24 of a day.
-- src:63 | pay period means
-- src:64 | (a) the usual period for which an employee is paid on a pay day, or
-- src:65 | (b) where there is no usual period, the period for which the employee is actually paid on a pay day,
-- src:66 | and for the purposes of paragraphs (a) and (b) includes a period of an hour or a day; (période de paie)
@ref Reg 3 "pay period" (src:63-66)
GIVEN `the usual period for which the employee is paid on a pay day, in days` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `the period for which the employee is actually paid on a pay day, in days` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`reg 3 — the length of the pay period, in days` `the usual period for which the employee is paid on a pay day, in days` `the period for which the employee is actually paid on a pay day, in days` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the usual period for which the employee is paid on a pay day, in days`
    WHEN JUST usual THEN usual
    WHEN NOTHING THEN `the period for which the employee is actually paid on a pay day, in days`

§§ `Regulation 5(5): the basic exemption for a pay period`

-- src:85 | (5) For the purposes of subsection (2), the amount of an employee’s basic exemption for each pay period in a year is
-- src:86 | (a) in the case of an employee who is ordinarily paid
-- src:87 | (i) hourly, $1.75,
-- src:88 | (ii) daily, $14.58,
-- src:89 | (iii) weekly, $67.30,
-- src:90 | (iv) bi-weekly, $134.61,
-- src:91 | (v) quadri-weekly, $269.23,
-- src:92 | (vi) semi-monthly, $145.83,
-- src:93 | (vii) monthly, $291.66,
-- src:94 | (viii) quarterly, $875,
-- src:95 | (ix) semi-annually, $1,750, or
-- src:96 | (x) annually, $3,500;
-- src:97 | (b) in the case of an employee who is ordinarily paid only in respect of a period of 10 months in the year and is paid
-- src:98 | (i) in 22 payments, $159.09,
-- src:99 | (ii) semi-monthly, $175, or
-- src:100 | (iii) monthly, $350; and
-- src:101 | (c) in any other case, the amount that is the greater of
-- src:102 | (i) the product obtained when $3,500 is multiplied by the fraction that the number of days in the period is of 365, and
-- src:103 | (ii) $67.30.
@ref Reg 5(5) (src:85-103)
GIVEN how IS A `cr1 How an employee is ordinarily paid`
      days IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`reg 5(5) — the employee's basic exemption for a pay period` how days MEANS
    CONSIDER how
    WHEN `paid hourly` THEN 1.75
    WHEN `paid daily` THEN 14.58
    WHEN `paid weekly` THEN 67.30
    WHEN `paid bi-weekly` THEN 134.61
    WHEN `paid quadri-weekly` THEN 269.23
    WHEN `paid semi-monthly` THEN 145.83
    WHEN `paid monthly` THEN 291.66
    WHEN `paid quarterly` THEN 875
    WHEN `paid semi-annually` THEN 1750
    WHEN `paid annually` THEN 3500
    WHEN `paid in 22 payments in respect of a period of 10 months in the year` THEN 159.09
    WHEN `paid semi-monthly in respect of a period of 10 months in the year` THEN 175
    WHEN `paid monthly in respect of a period of 10 months in the year` THEN 350
    WHEN `paid in any other way` THEN max ((3500 TIMES days) DIVIDED BY 365) 67.30

§§ `Regulation 5: the base and first additional contributions`

-- The rounding rule of subsection (2), used again in (3), (6)(c) and 5.1(2): the nearest multiple of $0.01
-- and, if two are equidistant, the higher. It also holds for a negative number: -0.285 rounds to -0.28.
-- src:76 | (2) Subject to subsections (6) to (8), the amount of an employee’s base contribution and an employee’s first additional contribution to be deducted by their employer from any qualifying payment of remuneration in a pay period in a year shall be determined using the following formula and rounding the result to the nearest multiple of $0.01 or, if that result is equidistant from two such multiples, to the higher of them:
@ref Reg 5(2) (src:76)
GIVEN amount IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`reg 5(2) — an amount rounded to the nearest multiple of $0.01, or the higher if two are equidistant` amount MEANS
    (FLOOR ((amount TIMES 100) PLUS 0.5)) DIVIDED BY 100

-- (1) a qualifying payment of remuneration is that portion of a payment of remuneration that is ordinary
-- remuneration from pensionable employment.
-- src:75 | 5 (1) For the purposes of this section, a qualifying payment of remuneration is that portion of a payment of remuneration that is ordinary remuneration from pensionable employment.
@ref Reg 5(1) (src:75)
GIVEN payment IS A `cr1 Payment of remuneration`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`reg 5(1) — the qualifying payment of remuneration` payment MEANS
    payment's `the part of the payment that is ordinary remuneration`

-- The rest of a payment of remuneration from pensionable employment is the portion that is not a qualifying
-- payment of remuneration, which subsection (3) deals with.
-- src:83 | (3) Subject to subsections (7) and (8), the amount of an employee’s base contribution and an employee’s first additional contribution in respect of that portion of a payment of remuneration from pensionable employment that is not a qualifying payment of remuneration is the product of that portion multiplied by the sum of the contribution rate for employees and the first additional contribution rate for employees for the year, rounded in the manner set out in subsection (2).
@ref Reg 5(3) (src:83)
GIVEN payment IS A `cr1 Payment of remuneration`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`reg 5(3) — the portion of a payment that is not a qualifying payment of remuneration` payment MEANS
    (payment's `the payment of remuneration from pensionable employment`)
    MINUS (`reg 5(1) — the qualifying payment of remuneration` payment)

-- (2) (A - B) x (C + D), rounded; A is the qualifying payment, B the exemption for the pay period, C the
-- contribution rate for employees and D the first additional contribution rate for employees. The formula
-- gives a negative number when A is less than B; subsections (6) and (3) are added to it before the total is
-- bounded below by nothing at all (fork F3).
-- src:76 | (2) Subject to subsections (6) to (8), the amount of an employee’s base contribution and an employee’s first additional contribution to be deducted by their employer from any qualifying payment of remuneration in a pay period in a year shall be determined using the following formula and rounding the result to the nearest multiple of $0.01 or, if that result is equidistant from two such multiples, to the higher of them:
-- src:77 | (A − B) × (C + D)
-- src:78 | where
-- src:79 | A is the qualifying payment of remuneration for the pay period;
-- src:80 | B is the employee’s basic exemption in respect of the pay period;
-- src:81 | C is the contribution rate for employees for the year; and
-- src:82 | D is the first additional contribution rate for employees for the year.
@ref Reg 5(2) (src:76-82)
GIVEN figures IS A `cr1 Figures the Act sets for a year`
      payment IS A `cr1 Payment of remuneration`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`reg 5(2) — the contribution on the qualifying payment of remuneration, before subsections (6) to (8)` figures payment MEANS
    `reg 5(2) — an amount rounded to the nearest multiple of $0.01, or the higher if two are equidistant`
        (  ((`reg 5(1) — the qualifying payment of remuneration` payment)
            MINUS (`reg 5(5) — the employee's basic exemption for a pay period` (payment's `how the employee is ordinarily paid`) (payment's `the number of days in the pay period`)))
         TIMES ((figures's `the contribution rate for employees`) PLUS (figures's `the first additional contribution rate for employees`)))

-- (3) the product of that portion multiplied by the sum of the two rates, rounded as in (2).
-- src:83 | (3) Subject to subsections (7) and (8), the amount of an employee’s base contribution and an employee’s first additional contribution in respect of that portion of a payment of remuneration from pensionable employment that is not a qualifying payment of remuneration is the product of that portion multiplied by the sum of the contribution rate for employees and the first additional contribution rate for employees for the year, rounded in the manner set out in subsection (2).
@ref Reg 5(3) (src:83)
GIVEN figures IS A `cr1 Figures the Act sets for a year`
      payment IS A `cr1 Payment of remuneration`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`reg 5(3) — the contribution on the portion that is not a qualifying payment of remuneration, before subsections (7) and (8)` figures payment MEANS
    `reg 5(2) — an amount rounded to the nearest multiple of $0.01, or the higher if two are equidistant`
        (  (`reg 5(3) — the portion of a payment that is not a qualifying payment of remuneration` payment)
         TIMES ((figures's `the contribution rate for employees`) PLUS (figures's `the first additional contribution rate for employees`)))

-- (6) If there are 27 bi-weekly or 53 weekly pay periods ending in a year, there is added, for each pay
-- period, to the contributions otherwise determined under subsection (2): (c) the product of the sum of the
-- two rates and the difference between (b) the exemption of subsection (5) and (a) the basic exemption for the
-- year divided by 27 or 53 ignoring amounts under $0.01, the product rounded as in (2).
-- src:104 | (6) If there are 27 bi-weekly or 53 weekly pay periods ending in a year, there shall be added to the employee’s contributions otherwise determined under subsection (2) for each pay period an amount equal to the amount determined when
-- src:105 | (a) the employee’s basic exemption for the year is divided by 27 or 53, as the case may be, without taking into consideration amounts less than $0.01;
-- src:106 | (b) the amount determined under paragraph (a) is subtracted from the amount of the applicable basic exemption determined under subsection (5); and
-- src:107 | (c) the amount determined under paragraph (b) is multiplied by the sum of the contribution rate for employees and the first additional contribution rate for employees for the year, and the product obtained is rounded to the nearest multiple of $0.01, or if that product is equidistant from two such multiples, to the higher of them.
@ref Reg 5(6) (src:104-107)
GIVEN figures IS A `cr1 Figures the Act sets for a year`
      payment IS A `cr1 Payment of remuneration`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`reg 5(6) — the amount added in a year with 27 bi-weekly or 53 weekly pay periods` figures payment MEANS
    CONSIDER (payment's `how the employee is ordinarily paid`)
    WHEN `paid bi-weekly` THEN
        IF (payment's `the number of pay periods ending in the year`) EQUALS 27
        THEN `reg 5(6) — the amount added for a divisor` figures payment 27
        ELSE 0
    WHEN `paid weekly` THEN
        IF (payment's `the number of pay periods ending in the year`) EQUALS 53
        THEN `reg 5(6) — the amount added for a divisor` figures payment 53
        ELSE 0
    OTHERWISE 0

@ref Reg 5(6) (src:104-107)
GIVEN figures IS A `cr1 Figures the Act sets for a year`
      payment IS A `cr1 Payment of remuneration`
      divisor IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`reg 5(6) — the amount added for a divisor` figures payment divisor MEANS
    `reg 5(2) — an amount rounded to the nearest multiple of $0.01, or the higher if two are equidistant`
        (  (  (`reg 5(5) — the employee's basic exemption for a pay period` (payment's `how the employee is ordinarily paid`) (payment's `the number of days in the pay period`))
            MINUS ((FLOOR (((figures's `the basic exemption`) DIVIDED BY divisor) TIMES 100)) DIVIDED BY 100))
         TIMES ((figures's `the contribution rate for employees`) PLUS (figures's `the first additional contribution rate for employees`)))

-- (7) If a payment of remuneration in respect of pensionable employment for a pay period exceeds the
-- employee's basic exemption for the pay period, the employee's contributions in respect of that payment are
-- at least $0.01.
-- src:108 | (7) If a payment of remuneration in respect of an employee’s pensionable employment for a pay period in a year exceeds the amount of the employee’s basic exemption for the pay period, the amount of the employee’s contributions in respect of that payment shall be at least $0.01.
@ref Reg 5(7) (src:108)
GIVEN payment IS A `cr1 Payment of remuneration`
      `the contribution otherwise determined` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`reg 5(7) — the contribution on a payment, with the minimum of $0.01` payment `the contribution otherwise determined` MEANS
    IF (payment's `the payment of remuneration from pensionable employment`)
       GREATER THAN (`reg 5(5) — the employee's basic exemption for a pay period` (payment's `how the employee is ordinarily paid`) (payment's `the number of days in the pay period`))
    THEN max `the contribution otherwise determined` 0.01
    ELSE `the contribution otherwise determined`

-- (6) of regulation 6: the contributions previously required to be deducted under a provincial pension plan
-- are counted at this Act's rates, by the ratio of the sum of this Act's two rates to the sum of the
-- provincial plan's corresponding rates. NOTHING when the provincial plan's rates sum to nothing, which the
-- text does not contemplate.
-- src:126 | 6 (1) If an employee has made a base contribution and a first additional contribution for the year under a provincial pension plan in respect of salary and wages paid to the employee by an employer, the amount of the employee’s base contribution and the employee’s first additional contribution determined under section 5, in respect of a payment of remuneration to the employee in that year by that employer, shall not exceed the amount remaining after subtracting from the sum of the year’s maximum base contribution and the year’s maximum first additional contribution the aggregate of that employee’s base contributions and first additional contributions previously required to be deducted in that year by that employer under this Part or under a provincial pension plan.
-- src:127 | (2) For the purposes of the calculation under subsection (1), the amount of contributions previously required to be deducted by the employer under a provincial pension plan is equal to the amount determined by multiplying the amount of those contributions by the ratio that the sum of the contribution rate for employees and the first additional contribution rate for employees under the Act bears to the sum of the corresponding rates of the provincial pension plan.
@ref Reg 6(1), 6(2) (src:126-127)
GIVEN figures IS A `cr1 Figures the Act sets for a year`
      provincial IS A `cr1 Provincial pension plan position`
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`reg 6(2) — the provincial plan's base and first additional contributions counted at this Act's rates` figures provincial MEANS
    IF NOT (provincial's `the employee has made contributions for the year under a provincial pension plan in respect of salary and wages paid by the employer`)
    THEN JUST 0
    ELSE IF (provincial's `sum of the provincial plan's contribution rate and first additional contribution rate for employees`) EQUALS 0
         THEN NOTHING
         ELSE JUST (  (provincial's `base and first additional contributions already required to be deducted under the provincial pension plan`)
                    TIMES (  ((figures's `the contribution rate for employees`) PLUS (figures's `the first additional contribution rate for employees`))
                           DIVIDED BY (provincial's `sum of the provincial plan's contribution rate and first additional contribution rate for employees`)))

-- (8) The aggregate of the employee's base and first additional contributions for a year deducted by an
-- employer shall not exceed the sum of the year's maximum base contribution and the year's maximum first
-- additional contribution; regulation 6(1) takes the provincial plan's contributions into the aggregate.
-- src:109 | (8) The aggregate of an employee’s base contributions and an employee’s first additional contributions for a year deducted by an employer in respect of pensionable employment with the employer shall not exceed the sum of the year’s maximum base contribution and the year’s maximum first additional contribution.
@ref Reg 5(8), 6(1) (src:109), (src:126)
GIVEN figures IS A `cr1 Figures the Act sets for a year`
      earlier IS A `cr1 Position earlier in the year`
      provincial IS A `cr1 Provincial pension plan position`
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`reg 5(8) — the room left under the limit on base and first additional contributions` figures earlier provincial MEANS
    CONSIDER `reg 6(2) — the provincial plan's base and first additional contributions counted at this Act's rates` figures provincial
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST counted THEN
        JUST (max 0 (  ((`reg 3 — the year's maximum base contribution` figures) PLUS (`reg 3 — the year's maximum first additional contribution` figures))
                     MINUS ((earlier's `base and first additional contributions already deducted under this Part`) PLUS counted)))

-- Regulations 4, 5 and 6 together: the base and first additional contributions the employer deducts from a
-- payment. (2) and (6) for the qualifying payment, (3) for the rest, the total bounded below at nothing (a
-- negative total is no deduction), the minimum of (7), and the limit of (8) last: where the limit leaves less
-- than $0.01 the limit governs (fork F4).
-- src:74 | 4 For the purposes of subsection 21(1) of the Act, the rules set out in sections 5 and 5.1 are prescribed for the purposes of determining an employee’s contribution to be deducted by the employee’s employer from any payment of remuneration in a year.
@ref Reg 4, 5(2), 5(3), 5(6), 5(7), 5(8), 6(1) (src:74)
GIVEN figures IS A `cr1 Figures the Act sets for a year`
      payment IS A `cr1 Payment of remuneration`
      earlier IS A `cr1 Position earlier in the year`
      provincial IS A `cr1 Provincial pension plan position`
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`reg 5 — the base and first additional contributions to deduct from a payment` figures payment earlier provincial MEANS
    CONSIDER `reg 5(8) — the room left under the limit on base and first additional contributions` figures earlier provincial
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST room THEN
        JUST (min room
                  (`reg 5(7) — the contribution on a payment, with the minimum of $0.01` payment
                      (max 0 (  (`reg 5(2) — the contribution on the qualifying payment of remuneration, before subsections (6) to (8)` figures payment)
                              PLUS (`reg 5(6) — the amount added in a year with 27 bi-weekly or 53 weekly pay periods` figures payment)
                              PLUS (`reg 5(3) — the contribution on the portion that is not a qualifying payment of remuneration, before subsections (7) and (8)` figures payment)))))

§§ `Regulation 5.1: the second additional contribution`

-- (1) For the year 2024 and each subsequent year, the second additional contribution is determined under
-- (2) when (A + B) - C exceeds zero: A the payment, B the total remuneration paid by the employer for the year
-- up to the date of the payment, C the greater of (a) that same total and (b) the maximum pensionable earnings.
-- src:110 | 5.1 (1) Subject to paragraph (3), for the year 2024 and each subsequent year, the amount of an employee’s second additional contribution to be deducted by their employer from a payment of remuneration paid to the employee in a year shall be determined in accordance with subsection (2) when the result of the following formula exceeds zero:
-- src:111 | (A + B) − C
-- src:112 | where
-- src:113 | A is the payment of remuneration that the employer pays to the employee;
-- src:114 | B is the total remuneration paid by the employer to that employee for the year up to the date of the payment; and
-- src:115 | C is the greater of
-- src:116 | (a) the total of the remuneration paid by the employer to that employee for the year up to the date of the payment; and
-- src:117 | (b) the amount of the employee’s maximum pensionable earnings for the year.
@ref Reg 5.1(1) (src:110-117)
GIVEN figures IS A `cr1 Figures the Act sets for a year`
      earlier IS A `cr1 Position earlier in the year`
      `the payment of remuneration that the employer pays to the employee` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`reg 5.1(1) — the result of the calculation` figures earlier `the payment of remuneration that the employer pays to the employee` MEANS
    (`the payment of remuneration that the employer pays to the employee`
     PLUS (earlier's `total remuneration the employer has already paid the employee in the year`))
    MINUS (max (earlier's `total remuneration the employer has already paid the employee in the year`)
               (figures's `the maximum pensionable earnings`))

-- (2) E x F, rounded as in regulation 5(2); E the result of (1) and F the second additional contribution rate
-- for employees for the year.
-- src:118 | (2) The amount of the employee’s second additional contribution is determined by using the following formula and rounding the result to the nearest multiple of $0.01 or, if that result is equidistant from two such multiples, to the higher of them:
-- src:119 | E × F
-- src:120 | where
-- src:121 | E is the result of the calculation as set out under subsection (1); and
-- src:122 | F is the second additional contribution rate for employees for the year.
@ref Reg 5.1(2) (src:118-122)
GIVEN figures IS A `cr1 Figures the Act sets for a year`
      `the result of the calculation under subsection (1)` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`reg 5.1(2) — the second additional contribution on the result` figures `the result of the calculation under subsection (1)` MEANS
    `reg 5(2) — an amount rounded to the nearest multiple of $0.01, or the higher if two are equidistant`
        (`the result of the calculation under subsection (1)` TIMES (figures's `the second additional contribution rate for employees`))

-- 6(4): the provincial plan's second additional contributions are counted at this Act's rate, by the ratio of
-- this Act's second additional contribution rate to the provincial plan's corresponding rate.
-- src:128 | (3) If an employee has made a second additional contribution for the year under a provincial pension plan in respect of salary and wages paid to the employee by an employer, the amount of the employee’s second additional contribution determined under section 5.1, in respect of a payment of remuneration to the employee in that year by that employer, shall not exceed the amount remaining after subtracting from the year’s maximum second additional contribution the aggregate of that employee’s second additional contributions previously required to be deducted in that year by that employer under this Part or under a provincial pension plan.
-- src:129 | (4) For the purposes of the calculation under subsection (3), the amount of contributions previously required to be deducted by the employer under a provincial pension plan is equal to the amount determined by multiplying the amount of those contributions by the ratio that the second additional contribution rate for employees under the Act bears to the corresponding rate under the provincial pension plan.
@ref Reg 6(3), 6(4) (src:128-129)
GIVEN figures IS A `cr1 Figures the Act sets for a year`
      provincial IS A `cr1 Provincial pension plan position`
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`reg 6(4) — the provincial plan's second additional contributions counted at this Act's rate` figures provincial MEANS
    IF NOT (provincial's `the employee has made contributions for the year under a provincial pension plan in respect of salary and wages paid by the employer`)
    THEN JUST 0
    ELSE IF (provincial's `the provincial plan's second additional contribution rate for employees`) EQUALS 0
         THEN NOTHING
         ELSE JUST (  (provincial's `second additional contributions already required to be deducted under the provincial pension plan`)
                    TIMES (  (figures's `the second additional contribution rate for employees`)
                           DIVIDED BY (provincial's `the provincial plan's second additional contribution rate for employees`)))

-- 5.1(3) with 6(3): the aggregate of second additional contributions for a year shall not exceed the year's
-- maximum second additional contribution, less what the provincial plan has taken (counted at this Act's rate).
-- src:123 | (3) The aggregate of an employee’s second additional contributions for a year deducted by the person’s employer from a payment of remuneration in respect of pensionable employment shall not exceed the year’s maximum second additional contribution.
@ref Reg 5.1(3), 6(3) (src:123), (src:128)
GIVEN figures IS A `cr1 Figures the Act sets for a year`
      earlier IS A `cr1 Position earlier in the year`
      provincial IS A `cr1 Provincial pension plan position`
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`reg 5.1(3) — the room left under the limit on second additional contributions` figures earlier provincial MEANS
    CONSIDER `reg 6(4) — the provincial plan's second additional contributions counted at this Act's rate` figures provincial
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST counted THEN
        JUST (max 0 (  (`reg 3 — the year's maximum second additional contribution` figures)
                     MINUS ((earlier's `second additional contributions already deducted under this Part`) PLUS counted)))

-- Regulations 5.1 and 6(3): the second additional contribution the employer deducts from a payment, from the
-- year 2024. Before 2024 the regulation says nothing (NOTHING). When the result of (1) does not exceed zero
-- there is nothing to determine and nothing is deducted.
-- src:110 | 5.1 (1) Subject to paragraph (3), for the year 2024 and each subsequent year, the amount of an employee’s second additional contribution to be deducted by their employer from a payment of remuneration paid to the employee in a year shall be determined in accordance with subsection (2) when the result of the following formula exceeds zero:
@ref Reg 5.1(1), 5.1(2), 5.1(3), 6(3) (src:110)
GIVEN year IS A NUMBER
      figures IS A `cr1 Figures the Act sets for a year`
      earlier IS A `cr1 Position earlier in the year`
      provincial IS A `cr1 Provincial pension plan position`
      `the payment of remuneration that the employer pays to the employee` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`reg 5.1 — the second additional contribution to deduct from a payment` year figures earlier provincial `the payment of remuneration that the employer pays to the employee` MEANS
    IF year LESS THAN 2024
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE CONSIDER `reg 5.1(3) — the room left under the limit on second additional contributions` figures earlier provincial
         WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
         WHEN JUST room THEN
             IF (`reg 5.1(1) — the result of the calculation` figures earlier `the payment of remuneration that the employer pays to the employee`) GREATER THAN 0
             THEN JUST (min room (`reg 5.1(2) — the second additional contribution on the result` figures (`reg 5.1(1) — the result of the calculation` figures earlier `the payment of remuneration that the employer pays to the employee`)))
             ELSE JUST 0

§§ `Regulations 3 and 4: the employee's contribution to deduct`

-- employee's contribution means any amount determined in accordance with sections 5, 5.1 and 6; and for the
-- purposes of subsection 21(1) of the Act the rules of sections 5 and 5.1 are prescribed for determining an
-- employee's contribution to be deducted by the employer from any payment of remuneration in a year.
-- src:59 | employee’s contribution means any amount determined in accordance with sections 5, 5.1 and 6; (cotisation de l’employé)
-- src:74 | 4 For the purposes of subsection 21(1) of the Act, the rules set out in sections 5 and 5.1 are prescribed for the purposes of determining an employee’s contribution to be deducted by the employee’s employer from any payment of remuneration in a year.
@ref Reg 3 "employee's contribution", Reg 4 (src:59), (src:74)
GIVEN year IS A NUMBER
      figures IS A `cr1 Figures the Act sets for a year`
      payment IS A `cr1 Payment of remuneration`
      earlier IS A `cr1 Position earlier in the year`
      provincial IS A `cr1 Provincial pension plan position`
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`reg 4 — the employee's contribution to deduct from a payment` year figures payment earlier provincial MEANS
    CONSIDER `reg 5 — the base and first additional contributions to deduct from a payment` figures payment earlier provincial
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST firstPart THEN
        CONSIDER `reg 5.1 — the second additional contribution to deduct from a payment` year figures earlier provincial (payment's `the payment of remuneration from pensionable employment`)
        WHEN NOTHING THEN
            IF year LESS THAN 2024 THEN JUST firstPart ELSE NOTHING
        WHEN JUST secondPart THEN JUST (firstPart PLUS secondPart)

§§ `Regulation 6.1: salary and wages on which a contribution was made under a provincial pension plan`

-- (1) the aggregate of all base contributions required to be made by the individual in the year under a
-- provincial pension plan in respect of salary and wages, divided by the base contribution rate for employees
-- under the provincial plan for the year. NOTHING when that rate is nil (the text does not contemplate it).
-- src:130 | 6.1 (1) For the purposes of subsections 10(1) and 13(3) of the Act, the salary and wages on which a base contribution has been made for the year by an individual under a provincial pension plan is an amount equal to the aggregate of all base contributions required to be made by the individual in that year under a provincial pension plan in respect of salary and wages, divided by the base contribution rate for employees under the provincial plan for the year.
@ref Reg 6.1(1) (src:130)
GIVEN `the aggregate of all base contributions required to be made by the individual in the year under a provincial pension plan` IS A NUMBER
      `the base contribution rate for employees under the provincial plan for the year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`reg 6.1(1) — the salary and wages on which a base contribution has been made under a provincial pension plan` `the aggregate of all base contributions required to be made by the individual in the year under a provincial pension plan` `the base contribution rate for employees under the provincial plan for the year` MEANS
    IF `the base contribution rate for employees under the provincial plan for the year` EQUALS 0
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE JUST (`the aggregate of all base contributions required to be made by the individual in the year under a provincial pension plan`
               DIVIDED BY `the base contribution rate for employees under the provincial plan for the year`)

-- src:131 | (2) For the purposes of subsections 10(1.1) and 13(3.1) and (3.2) of the Act, the salary and wages on which a first additional contribution has been made for the year by an individual under a provincial pension plan is an amount equal to the aggregate of all first additional contributions required to be made by the individual in that year under a provincial pension plan in respect of salary and wages, divided by the first additional contribution rate for employees under the provincial pension plan for the year.
@ref Reg 6.1(2) (src:131)
GIVEN `the aggregate of all first additional contributions required to be made by the individual in the year under a provincial pension plan` IS A NUMBER
      `the first additional contribution rate for employees under the provincial pension plan for the year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`reg 6.1(2) — the salary and wages on which a first additional contribution has been made under a provincial pension plan` `the aggregate of all first additional contributions required to be made by the individual in the year under a provincial pension plan` `the first additional contribution rate for employees under the provincial pension plan for the year` MEANS
    IF `the first additional contribution rate for employees under the provincial pension plan for the year` EQUALS 0
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE JUST (`the aggregate of all first additional contributions required to be made by the individual in the year under a provincial pension plan`
               DIVIDED BY `the first additional contribution rate for employees under the provincial pension plan for the year`)

-- src:132 | (3) For the purposes of subsections 10(1.2) and 13(3.2) of the Act, the salary and wages on which a second additional contribution has been made for the year by an individual under a provincial pension plan is an amount equal to the aggregate of all second additional contributions required to be made by the individual in that year under a provincial pension plan in respect of salary and wages, divided by the second additional contribution rate for employees under the provincial pension plan for the year.
@ref Reg 6.1(3) (src:132)
GIVEN `the aggregate of all second additional contributions required to be made by the individual in the year under a provincial pension plan` IS A NUMBER
      `the second additional contribution rate for employees under the provincial pension plan for the year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`reg 6.1(3) — the salary and wages on which a second additional contribution has been made under a provincial pension plan` `the aggregate of all second additional contributions required to be made by the individual in the year under a provincial pension plan` `the second additional contribution rate for employees under the provincial pension plan for the year` MEANS
    IF `the second additional contribution rate for employees under the provincial pension plan for the year` EQUALS 0
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE JUST (`the aggregate of all second additional contributions required to be made by the individual in the year under a provincial pension plan`
               DIVIDED BY `the second additional contribution rate for employees under the provincial pension plan for the year`)

§§ `Regulation 7: the employer's contribution`

-- employer's contribution means an amount determined in accordance with section 7; and section 7: the amount
-- an employer shall remit as the employer's contribution in respect of a payment of remuneration to an
-- employee in pensionable employment is an amount equal to the employee's contributions required to be
-- deducted under this Part in respect of that payment.
-- src:60 | employer’s contribution means an amount determined in accordance with section 7; (cotisation de l’employeur)
-- src:135 | 7 The amount that an employer shall remit as the employer’s contribution in respect of a payment of remuneration made by the employer to an employee in pensionable employment is an amount equal to the employee’s contributions required to be deducted under this Part in respect of that payment of remuneration.
@ref Reg 3 "employer's contribution", Reg 7 (src:60), (src:135)
GIVEN `the employee's contributions required to be deducted under this Part in respect of the payment` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`reg 7 — the employer's contribution to remit in respect of a payment` `the employee's contributions required to be deducted under this Part in respect of the payment` MEANS
    `the employee's contributions required to be deducted under this Part in respect of the payment`
